axe-helper.ts:19-41 - The helper manually splits results.violations
into serious/critical vs minor arrays, reconstructs { violations:
critical }, and passes the partial object to toHaveNoViolations().
This works but relies on jest-axe's private object shape.

The idiomatic approach:
  import { configureAxe, toHaveNoViolations } from "jest-axe";
  const axe = configureAxe({ impactLevels: ["serious", "critical"] });
  expect(await axe(container)).toHaveNoViolations();

The helper becomes a clean two-liner; jest-axe handles the filtering
internally and is not coupled to the violation object shape.
